# How to cite Lutefisk Book Editor. GitHub reads this file and shows a
# "Cite this repository" button (APA and BibTeX) on the repository page.
# Spec: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Lutefisk Book Editor in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Lutefisk Book Editor"
abstract: >-
  A local-first book writing and formatting studio with live device and print
  previews. Write, design and export books (EPUB, PDF, Word, RTF, MOBI,
  Markdown and plain text) entirely on your own computer — no accounts, no
  cloud, no tracking.
authors:
  - given-names: "John L."
    family-names: "Whiteman"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/johnlwhiteman/lutefisk-book-editor"
url: "https://github.com/johnlwhiteman/lutefisk-book-editor#readme"
keywords:
  - book editor
  - writing
  - self-publishing
  - ebook
  - epub
  - pdf
  - typesetting
  - electron
  - local-first
